<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puttalam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Puttalam is a town on the north-west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, on the Puttalam Lagoon. The nearby coast is one of the places linked by tradition with the landing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-vijaya">Prince Vijaya</a>, and the area has long been known for its salt pans and coconut plantations. The town has a large Muslim community with old trading connections.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/puttalam.jpg" alt="Puttalam" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vincent van Zeijst · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sri_Lanka,_Puttalam_street_scene_(5).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
